WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.720
It may seem like everyone wants to be a superhero
these days, but a few stars have still tried

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:08.220
to steer clear of the world of comic book
movies.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.740
Here are a few of the actors who said no when
DC came calling.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:17.360
Leonardo DiCaprio has spent the vast majority
of his life in Hollywood, but before he achieved

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.609
global fame in James Cameron's 1997 epic Titanic,
Warner Brothers.

00:00:21.609 --> 00:00:24.520
approached him to star in Joel Schumacher's
Batman Forever.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.560
Seeing how things turned out, it's probably
fair to say that turning them down was the

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.420
right choice.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:34.670
The studio wanted DiCaprio for the part of
Dick Grayson, also known as Robin, but DiCaprio

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.820
just wasn't feeling it.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.600
Contrary to rumors, DiCaprio has said he never
screen-tested for the role, though he did

00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.720
talk to Schumacher.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:42.720
He told Shortlist:

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.500
"I had a meeting with Joel Schumacher.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.860
It was just one meeting and, no, I didn't
end up doing it."

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:52.520
Despite meeting with the director, DiCaprio
said he never even wanted the role.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.320
He explained:

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.580
"As I recall I took the meeting but didn't
want to play the role.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.820
Joel Schumacher is a very talented director,
but I don't think I was ready for anything

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:01.340
like that."

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:06.100
The role ended up going to Chris O'Donnell,
but, interestingly, Robin wasn't the only

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:10.890
superhero role Hollywood offered DiCaprio,
Sony Pictures approached him to play Spider-Man

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.160
for director Sam Raimi.

00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.680
But as with Robin, he said he just wasn't
ready to put on a suit.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:20.380
At this juncture in his Oscar-winning career,
it seems unlikely he's in any rush to change

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:20.880
his mind.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.980
Warner Brothers had been trying to get a Green
Lantern film off the ground for well over

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.820
a decade before Martin Campbell directed the
character's first live-action outing in 2011.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.420
The studio approached Kevin Smith in 1997
to write a script for the film, but he turned

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:38.280
down the offer, feeling he wasn't the right
fit for the job.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:42.740
Then renowned director Quentin Tarantino received
an offer to helm the project, but he also

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:46.240
turned it down, feeling he'd outgrown his
adoration for comic books.

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:50.720
When the studio finally settled on a director
and screenwriter, they began their search

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:51.700
for Hal Jordan.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.020
While Ryan Reynolds ultimately got the part,
he wasn't always the top contender.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:02:00.770
Warner Brothers approached Bradley Cooper,
Chris Pine, Justin Timberlake, and Sam Worthington,

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.480
who all either turned the role down or were
rejected by the studio.

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:07.380
Another one-time contender was Mad Men star
Jon Hamm.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.940
He recalled to GQ:

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:11.440
"They came after me pretty hard for Green
Lantern.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.720
But I was like, 'Meh, that's not what I want
to do.'

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.520
Never say never, but these aren't the kind
of movies I like to go and see.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.770
They don't make the kind of movies I like
to see anymore."

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:21.580
"Nostalgia.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.180
It's delicate, but potent."

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:35.380
Pierce Brosnan has had a hugely prolific career,
but his tenure as the slick MI6 spy James

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:37.920
Bond will undoubtedly remain its highlight.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.640
At one point, however, Brosnan had the opportunity
to star in a comic book movie that probably

00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:47.230
would have not only dashed his chances to
be Bond, but also changed the landscape of

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:49.260
the superhero genre altogether.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:55.140
Just imagine for a second that Brosnan, not
Michael Keaton, played Batman in Tim Burton's

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.260
1989 film.

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.600
Sounds crazy, but there was a chance of it
happening.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:02.600
In a Reddit AMA, Brosnan admitted to meeting
Burton for the role.

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:03.240
He wrote:

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.620
"Yes, I did.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.860
I went and met with Tim Burton for the role
of Batman.

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:11.340
But I just couldn't really take it seriously,
any man who wears his underpants outside his

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.740
pants just cannot be taken seriously.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.160
That was my foolish take on it.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.460
It was a joke, I thought.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:17.900
But how wrong was I?"

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.000
Brosnan stressed the fact that he doesn't
hate Batman, he just couldn't see himself

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.420
playing the character in a movie.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.160
He wrote:

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.960
"Don't get me wrong, because I love Batman,
and I grew up on Batman.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:32.060
As a kid in Ireland, we used to get our raincoats
and tie them round our neck and swing through

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:33.090
the bicycle shed."

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.840
However, it appears that Brosnan's hesitation
with Batman led him to James Bond, and thus

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.280
gave him the defining role of his career.

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:41.500
So it's not all bad.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.620
There aren't many actors more highly regarded
than Anthony Hopkins.

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:50.060
Known to many as Hannibal Lecter from The
Silence of the Lambs and its sequels, Hopkins

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:55.160
was also up for a few early roles in the world
of comic book movies, but declined to take

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:55.660
them.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:04:00.840
Before Michael Caine boarded Christopher Nolan's
Batman Begins as Bruce Wayne's butler, Alfred

00:04:00.850 --> 00:04:03.850
Pennyworth, Nolan reportedly offered Hopkins
the role.

00:04:03.850 --> 00:04:06.260
He turned it down, however, for reasons unknown.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:11.520
Interestingly, despite reportedly being turned
down for the role of Mr. Freeze in Joel Schumacher's

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:15.460
Batman &amp; Robin, Hopkins maintained his interest
in DC movies.

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:20.120
Not long after turning down the role of Alfred
Pennyworth in Batman Begins, he finally joined

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:25.540
the DC universe as Jor-El in J.J. Abrams and
Brett Ratner's Superman: Flyby.

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:30.560
Things didn't work out, though, and the project
mutated into Bryan Singer's Superman Returns.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:31.780
He told MTV News:

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:34.680
"I was going to do the movie with Brett, and
I don't know what happened.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.460
[There was] some political movement.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:39.510
I think Brett was out of line with something
and they said thank you very much.

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.820
I never heard from Brett since then, but I
was all set to do it."

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:47.850
Hopkins finally found his comic book home
in 2011, when he took the role of Odin in

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.340
Thor; a role he has returned to many times
since.

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:55.960
Jude Law may be an excellent actor, but he's
not really a huge movie star.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:05:00.380
After the disastrous critical and box office
performance of Sky Captain &amp; The World of

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:05.070
Tomorrow, Law was probably nervous about headlining
another action franchise, especially when

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.630
the character in question was the greatest
superhero of them all.

00:05:08.630 --> 00:05:12.740
On The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, Law
revealed that director Bryan Singer offered

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:16.380
him the role of the Man of Steel for 2006's
Superman Returns.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.320
"I have this picture of that, of me in that
costume.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.400
You know, posters all around the world, and
I was like, 'No way.'"

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.780
Law turned down the role, which went to the
relatively unknown Brandon Routh.

00:05:26.860 --> 00:05:31.520
After Superman Returns' lukewarm reception,
the series was rebooted with Law's fellow

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.500
Brit, Henry Cavill, taking the lead.

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:37.680
"I'm an Englishman, and, you know, it felt
like, it just didn't seem to fit.

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:41.340
And I was worried about the outfit, and I
just didn't fancy it."

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.380
Law presumably had no such qualms about the
wardrobe attached to the character of Yon-Rogg,

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:50.880
the Kree warrior he played in 2019's MCU blockbuster
Captain Marvel.

00:05:51.560 --> 00:05:55.780
Movie stars don't come much bigger than Will
Smith, and this was especially true in the

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:56.870
mid-2000s.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:06:00.110
So it seemed natural that he'd end up taking
a part in a superhero movie.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:05.140
And, according to Smith himself, he wasn't
just offered any superhero role, but the mightiest

00:06:05.140 --> 00:06:06.740
of them all: Superman.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.710
Apparently, Bryan Singer asked Smith to play
the big blue boy scout in Superman Returns.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:13.500
But Smith didn't even need to see the suit.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.520
He rejected the part because he didn't want
to repeat what was then his biggest career

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:18.020
mistake.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.520
Smith told MTV:

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.640
"'There is no way I'm playing Superman!'

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:26.400
Because I had already done Jim West [in Wild
Wild West], and you can't be messing up white

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:28.160
people's heroes in Hollywood.

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:31.800
You mess up white people's heroes in Hollywood,
you'll never work in this town again!"

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:37.420
Smith would go on to play his own superhero
in Hancock, and would later join the DC Expanded

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.120
Universe as Deadshot.

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:44.700
Imagine living in an alternate universe where
Heath Ledger played Batman and Christian Bale

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.710
played the Joker.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.060
Well, it's not really that far-fetched.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:52.540
In 2005, Ledger was Hollywood's gravelly voiced
king of cool, while Bale was most known for

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:56.920
playing the maniacal murdering psychopath
Patrick Bateman in American Psycho.

00:06:57.040 --> 00:07:00.960
And according to the Dark Knight Trilogy's
director Christopher Nolan, it was almost

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:03.820
Ledger, not Bale, who donned the cape and
cowl.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:07.590
In an interview with the Daily Star, Nolan
revealed that he offered the part of Batman

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.220
to Ledger but was turned down.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:10.300
Nolan said:

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.919
"He was quite gracious about it, but he said,
'I would never take a part in a superhero

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:14.420
film.'"

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:19.370
Thankfully, Ledger eventually changed his
mind, presumably after he saw Batman Begins

00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:23.520
and realized Nolan was going for a grittier,
more realistic take on the character.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:27.880
Fortunately, there were no hard feelings on
Nolan's end, as he clearly was a great admirer

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:28.840
of Ledger's work.

00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:32.340
The Dark Knight would go on to be one of the
highest-grossing movies of the decade, being

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:38.210
the first film to earn over $500 million domestically
since Titanic, largely due to Ledger's performance

00:07:38.210 --> 00:07:40.040
as the Clown Prince of Crime.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:45.540
Ledger tragically died before the film's release,
but his work won him his first and only Oscar.

00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:50.520
It seems like everybody was considered for
the part of Wonder Woman at some time or another,

00:07:50.520 --> 00:07:53.910
though it's doubtful many of the actresses
considered were ever formally approached for

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:54.400
the role.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:58.040
One actress who was approached, and turned
it down, was Kate Beckinsale.

00:07:58.280 --> 00:08:03.420
With her lead role as vampire death dealer
Selene in the successful Underworld franchise,

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.340
Beckinsale would have been a perfect fit for
the Amazonian warrior in the mid-2000s.

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:12.300
Alas, the most recent female superheroes on
film during that time were Halle Berry in

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.760
Catwoman, Jennifer Garner in Elektra, and
Charlize Theron in Aeon Flux.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.840
Not the best track record, and it sounds like
this proposed Wonder Woman vehicle wasn't

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:21.820
going to be much better.

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:26.540
Speaking in reference to 2017's Wonder Woman,
Beckinsale later told Yahoo Movies:

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:30.360
"The incarnations that I was seeing were…They
weren't this one."

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:34.600
But even if the script had been better, it
sounds like Beckinsale would have been hung

00:08:34.610 --> 00:08:38.620
up by the same thing which has always worried
actors playing superheroes.

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:39.620
Beckinsale explained:

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:42.040
"I don't know if I was desperate to be in
a leotard.

00:08:42.160 --> 00:08:43.660
I'd already done the rubber trousers.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.840
You have to take in that you have a child
at some point and how much could you possibly

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.560
embarrass them?"

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:54.100
Charlize Theron wasn't up for the part of
Wonder Woman in the 2017 film, but she did

00:08:54.110 --> 00:08:57.490
turn down a major role as Wonder Woman's mother,
Hippolyta.

00:08:57.490 --> 00:09:02.300
In an interview with Andy Cohen on Watch What
Happens Live!, Theron explained she ended

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:05.610
up in talks for a part in the movie while
it was still in development, but it wasn't

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:06.620
the one she expected.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.560
"And I was like, 'I'm just, I'm not familiar
with it.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:12.170
I don't really know, I mean, what does Wonder
Woman do?'

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:16.480
And at this point my, this person said, 'No,
it's for Wonder Woman's mom.'"

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.600
Theron, of course, is only ten years older
than Wonder Woman star Gal Gadot.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:26.180
Despite Wonder Woman being directed by Patty
Jenkins, who directed Charlize Theron's Oscar-winning

00:09:26.190 --> 00:09:31.230
turn in 2003's Monster, Theron declined the
part, which went to Connie Nielsen, who is

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:33.360
about 19 years older than Gadot.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:38.520
Director Zack Snyder apparently felt "slighted"
when Kristen Stewart rejected the role of

00:09:38.520 --> 00:09:40.800
Lois Lane in 2013's Man of Steel.

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:45.180
According to sources close to the director,
he and his wife/producing partner Deborah

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.420
met with Stewart about playing the iconic
reporter.

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:51.760
While Snyder was interested in Stewart, however,
he apparently never formally offered her the

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:52.260
part.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.740
But Stewart made clear that she was not interested,
evidently surprising Snyder.

00:09:56.880 --> 00:10:01.020
Stewart herself had been caught "off-guard"
by the blockbuster success of the Twilight

00:10:01.029 --> 00:10:05.500
films and the spotlight it put on her personal
life, especially her relationship with co-star

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:06.500
Robert Pattinson.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:10.040
Stewart was still working on the Twilight
series at the time and wanted to focus on

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:14.140
smaller, more independent films, which Man
of Steel most definitely was not.

00:10:14.260 --> 00:10:19.400
Snyder wasn't upset for long, however, and
soon hired A-lister Amy Adams for the role.

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:23.010
But Adams may have wished she'd turned down
the part too.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:28.010
Stewart's focus on smaller films gave her
career a renewed vigor, while Snyder's DC

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:31.920
films started with poor feedback and continued
on a downward slide.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.920
Maybe Stewart ought to warn her ex before
he puts on that cowl as the new Batman!

